          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ચૂનો",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ચૂનો — cūno — \"lime wash\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દિવાળી પહેલાં અમે દીવાલો પર ચૂનો લગાડીએ છીએ. divāḷī pahelā̃ ame dīvālo par cūno lagāḍīe chīe. Before Diwali we put lime wash on the walls."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ચૂનો (cūno) is a tadbhava, inherited from Sanskrit cūrṇa, \"powder\", and CDIAL lists the Gujarati word as \"lime\" (CDIAL 4889)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
